SUMMARY:Chicken
DESCRIPTION:Don Murphy is a proud Irishman\, a hopeless addict\, and one of his generation’s greatest actors. He also happens to be a chicken… \nOver one fateful night\, the feathered Oscar-winner shares his star-studded story with an intimate audience — from his big break\, to his first bird-on-bird sexual experience\, to navigating life in the (human-dominated) celebrity spotlight. But along the way\, Don will be confronted with some harsh truths about himself\, chickenkind and humankind. \n“This show where a woman who plays a chicken who thinks he’s an Irishman is unlike anything you’ve ever seen.” — Playbill \nThis play is part of the Canada Ireland Foundation’s Bealtaine Theatre Festival\, which brings the best of Irish Theatre to Toronto. An annual celebration\, the Bealtaine Theatre Festival features Canadian premieres of some of Ireland’s most captivating and contemporary theatre. Bealtaine will be held May 21 to June 7 at the Corleck — a brand new performance venue on Toronto’s waterfront. Learn more. \nCHICKENby Sunday’s Child TheatreCo-written by Eva O’Connor and Hildegard RyanDirected by Hildegard RyanFeaturing Eva O’Connor \nRecommended for Ages 13+
URL:https://nowtoronto.com/event/chicken/
LOCATION:The Corleck Building\, 3 Eireann Quay\, Toronto\, ON M5V 0A3\, Canada\, Old Toronto\, Toronto\, Ontario\, M5V 0A3
CATEGORIES:Performing Arts,Theatre & Opera
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/png:https://nowtoronto.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/03/chicken.png
END:VEVENT
