SUMMARY:Her Sports Fest
DESCRIPTION:A new\, hands-on celebration of girls and women in sport is coming to Toronto this spring. The inaugural Her Sports Fest will take place May 22–24\, 2026 at The Hangar Sport and Events Centre in Downsview Park\, bringing together girls and women of all ages for a dynamic\, action-packed weekend designed to get more girls and women active in sport. \nBuilt around four core themes — “Try It. Learn It. Find It. Amp It.” — Her Sports Fest offers an inclusive\, interactive space where participants can discover new sports\, build skills\, connect with others\, and celebrate their journey in sport. On-site activations and live demonstrations will feature a range of sports — including biathlon\, flag football\, soccer\, golf\, skateboarding\, athletics\, sailing and many more. \nHer Sports Fest will feature a “Learn It” Chalk Talk series with athletes\, coaches and experts\, alongside a “Find It” marketplace showcasing leading brands and the latest gear and equipment. Elite-level athlete appearances throughout the weekend will highlight personal journeys and the impact of sport on both mental and physical well-being. Full schedule of appearances and Chalk Talks will be announced in the lead-up to the event.
URL:https://nowtoronto.com/event/her-sports-fest/
LOCATION:The Hangar\, 75 Carl Hall Rd #1001A\, North York\, ON M3K 2B9\, Canada\, North York\, Toronto\, Ontario\, M3K 2B9
CATEGORIES:Community Events,Festivals,Sports
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/png:https://nowtoronto.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/04/her-sports-fest.png
END:VEVENT
